HealthConnect aims to improve patient appointment attendance and healthcare support by using data and AI. Missed appointments (no-shows) can affect healthcare service delivery and the efficient use of available appointment slots. Therefore, the project focuses on understanding appointment attendance patterns and identifying factors that may be associated with patients missing their scheduled appointments.
The available appointment data will be examined to determine whether it can support a machine-learning solution for predicting appointment no-shows. The analysis will provide a foundation for identifying relevant features, defining the prediction target, and developing an appropriate modelling approach. The ultimate goal is to provide information that can support better appointment management and help healthcare services make more informed decisions.
